      porQueImporta: 'If the country\'s only centre halts or saturates, there is nowhere to refer patients: PET-CT helps define whether a cancer treatment continues, changes or stops. That the scan is free for the patient does not remove the question of how much the State pays for each one, and under what agreement.',
      caveat: 'PET-CT funding is channelled through an agreement between the FNR —a non-state public entity— and CUDIM, not through an open tender, so it is unlikely to appear in the state procurement search. The sources consulted do not report the per-scan price the Fund pays. IMPO\'s "more than 16,000 studies" figure is cumulative and its page is undated.',
